ZFM-derived document core and rendering adapters
------------------------------------------------
The semantic reader was adapted from ZFM native/documents at revision
9d69a973fb0b6f5242295c52513c1dfc1f6f5dde. Its pinned crate manifest declares MIT,
while its pinned repository supplies the GNU GPL version 3 text. The relationship
between those declarations remains unresolved here; no governing license or
relicense is asserted. Both pieces of evidence are retained unchanged:

  native/documents/UPSTREAM.json
  native/documents/LICENSE-ZFM
  native/documents/Cargo.toml
  app/src/main/assets/document-notices.txt

The bounded visual adapter, memory-limit launcher, Android font discovery and
mobile rendering patches also originate in ZFM. Their recorded provenance and
local adaptations are retained in:

  native/render/README.md
  native/render/zfm-provenance.json
  native/render/core/
  native/render/patches/

AllDoc's root Apache grant excludes these ZFM-derived contributions. Publishing
this source tree does not resolve the upstream scope question. Distributors must
retain the applicable notices and provide corresponding source as required by the
applicable licenses; an Apache-only or MIT-only claim for the combined binary is
not made here.

Craft engines and fonts
-----------------------
WordCraft, DeckCraft and GridCraft are pinned Git submodules from
https://github.com/storytold. Selected parser/rendering code uses the upstream MIT
option where dual-licensed. Local mobile patches are kept outside the submodules.
Font and asset licenses are separate, including SIL OFL-1.1 and Ubuntu Font License.
Their original license, copyright and attribution texts are retained in:

  .gitmodules
  native/render/notices/
  native/render/office-fonts/LICENSE
  native/render/zfm-provenance.json
  app/src/main/assets/render-notices.txt

Other dependencies
------------------
The OACP Android SDK is Apache-2.0, pinned without source modifications. Its exact
revision and source hashes are in oacp-sdk/UPSTREAM.json; its complete license is
in oacp-sdk/src/main/assets/oacp-sdk-license.txt.

AndroidX, Compose, Kotlin and other application dependencies retain their own
licenses. The resolved application inventory and bundled notices are in
app/src/main/assets/application-notices.txt.

Native dependencies retain their declared licenses, including MPL-2.0 for
nucleo-matcher. Exact versions, source locations and full license/notice texts are
retained in native/documents/dependencies-upstream.json, native/pdf/dependencies-upstream.json,
native/render/dependencies-upstream.json and each component's notices directory.
The app includes document-notices.txt, pdf-notices.txt and render-notices.txt.

Examples and design references
------------------------------
Bundled examples and AllDoc-authored artwork use its original-work
license. Their provenance and generators are documented in scripts/text-examples.md
and scripts/fixtures/EXAMPLES-OFFICE.md. The separate scripts/fixtures/simple.doc
